  "tagline": "Pure-Go embedded key-value store with Bitcask storage and Redis-like lists, sets and sorted sets.",
  "description": "NutsDB is an embeddable, persistent key-value store written in pure Go that uses a Bitcask-style append-only log with an in-memory index, giving fast writes and single-seek reads. Beyond plain buckets it offers Redis-like data structures (lists, sets and sorted sets), per-key TTLs and fully serializable transactions, which makes it convenient for Go services that want Redis-ish semantics without a server. Because the index is held in memory, the number of keys is bounded by RAM, and merges must be run to reclaim space.",
